# sluice — reverse .gitignore (deny-all allowlist).
#
# Everything is ignored by default; only paths explicitly re-included with `!`
# below are tracked. This is a CURATED whitelist: a brand-new file is invisible
# to git until you add a `!` rule for it. That is the point — nothing is
# committed by accident. The tradeoff is that each new tracked path is a
# deliberate one-line decision here.

# 1) Ignore everything.
*

# 2) ...but let git descend into directories so the `!file` rules below can
#    reach nested files. Directories re-ignored in section 3 are still skipped.
!*/

# 3) Never track these, even when a rule below would otherwise match: real
#    config, secrets, pipeline state, logs, caches, environments, OS cruft.
.pixi/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.venv/
config.json
config.*.json
.env
.env.*
secrets/
data/
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
logs/
*.log
.DS_Store
*.swp
*~
.idea/
.vscode/

# 4) Packaging, CI, and top-level project metadata.
!/.gitignore
!/pixi.toml
!/pixi.lock
!/install.sh
!/README.md
!/HANDOFF.md
!/CONTEXT.md
!/config.example.json
!/.github/workflows/*.yml

# 5) The Python project — source and tests, matched by extension so caches and
#    byte-compiled files are never swept in.
!/sluice/**/*.py
!/tests/**/*.py

# 6) Guardrail tooling. The hooks and their wiring are tracked because they must
#    sync to the CHTC copy to protect production there too (HANDOFF §9b).
#    NOT the agents — you curate those yourself; add one line per agent you want,
#    e.g.  !/.claude/agents/plan-author.md
!/.claude/README.md
!/.claude/settings.json
!/.claude/hooks/*.py
!/.claude/skills/**/*.md

# 7) Docs: build plans and the analysis notes. The design SPECS under
#    /docs/superpowers/plans are tracked because they are the source of truth
#    for the plans.
!/docs/superpowers/plans/*.md

#    The ADRs are tracked (added 2026-08-01, plan 14 follow-up). Commits have
#    cited them by name since 0001 while the files existed only on one laptop.
#    They are also load-bearing tooling: /improve-codebase-architecture reads
#    docs/adr/ to know which decisions NOT to re-litigate, so an untracked ADR
#    stops suppressing settled suggestions the moment a second copy exists.
#    Contain decisions and reasoning only — no config values, no secrets.
!/docs/adr/*.md

#    Operator- and contributor-facing docs at the /docs ROOT (added 2026-08-02).
#    A glob rather than one line per file, deliberately: docs/OPERATING.md was
#    written on 2026-08-02 for the colleague who will run sluice unattended, the
#    commit that "added" it (564bf5b) recorded it as landed, and the deny-all
#    rule silently swallowed it — the single most handover-critical document in
#    the repo existed on one laptop for a day without anyone noticing. Non-
#    recursive on purpose: docs/superpowers/, docs/dev-cycle/, docs/teachme/ and
#    docs/agents/ stay untracked, so this admits only the small set of top-level
#    guides. Anything placed here is operator-readable by definition — no config
#    values, no secrets, same standard as the ADRs.
!/docs/*.md

#    Design specs are allowlisted ONE FILE AT A TIME, never by glob: the errata
#    and the design of record in that directory carry production values (the
#    gate map needed redaction before it could be committed in 8cb03ef), so a
#    `!/docs/superpowers/specs/*.md` rule would sweep them in unreviewed. Each
#    line below is a spec that has been scanned clean.
!/docs/superpowers/specs/2026-08-02-sluice-doctor-design.md

# 8) Ruff linting
!/ruff.toml

